370	374	339	339	He	125	" Mr Midshipman Easy "
1172	1185	1186	1186	he	129	" thought , good easy man , that his greatness was ripening ; "
1464	1472	1462	1462	Shakespeare	130	" the pleasing punishment that women bear ; "
1486	1493	1474	1475	Mrs Easy	131	" that all men were liars , "
1607	1627	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" I have been thinking , my dear Mrs Easy , about the name I shall give this child . "
1628	1646	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" Name , Mr Easy ! why , what name should you give it but your own ? "
1647	1654	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" Not so , my dear , "
1659	1685	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" they call all names proper names , but I think that mine is not . It is the very worst name in the calendar . "
1686	1699	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" Why , what 's the matter with it , Mr Easy ? "
1700	1760	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" The matter affects me as well as the boy . Nicodemus is a long name to write at full length , and Nick is vulgar . Besides , as there will be two Nicks , they will naturally call my boy young Nick , and of course I shall be styled old Nick , which will be diabolical . "
1761	1777	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" Well , Mr Easy , at all events then let me choose the name . "
1778	1801	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" That you shall , my dear , and it was with this view that I have mentioned the subject so early . "
1802	1825	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" I think , Mr Easy , I will call the boy after my poor father -- his name shall be Robert . "
1826	1872	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" Very well , my dear , if you wish it , it shall be Robert . You shall have your own way . But I think , my dear , upon a little consideration , you will acknowledge that there is a decided objection . "
1873	1880	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" An objection , Mr Easy ? "
1881	1909	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" Yes , my dear ; Robert may be very well , but you must reflect upon the consequences ; he is certain to be called Bob . "
1910	1924	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" Well , my dear , and suppose they do call him Bob ? "
1925	1953	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" I can not bear even the supposition , my dear . You forget the county in which we are residing , the downs covered with sheep . "
1954	1971	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" Why , Mr Easy , what can sheep have to do with a Christian name ? "
1972	2161	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" There it is ; women never look to consequences . My dear , they have a great deal to do with the name of Bob . I will appeal to any farmer in the county , if ninety - nine shepherds ' dogs out of one hundred are not called Bob . Now observe , your child is out of doors somewhere in the fields or plantations ; you want and you call him . Instead of your child , what do you find ? Why , a dozen curs at least , who come running up to you , all answering to the name of Bob , and wagging their stumps of tails . You see , Mrs Easy , it is a dilemma not to be got over . You level your only son to the brute creation by giving him a Christian name which , from its peculiar brevity , has been monopolised by all the dogs in the county . Any other name you please , my dear , but in this one instance you must allow me to lay my positive veto . "
2162	2189	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" Well , then , let me see -- but I 'll think of it , Mr Easy ; my head aches very much just now . "
2190	2207	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" I will think for you , my dear . What do you say to John ? "
2208	2221	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" Oh , no , Mr Easy , such a common name ? "
2222	2281	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" A proof of its popularity , my dear . It is scriptural -- we have the apostle and the baptist -- we have a dozen popes who were all Johns . It is royal -- we have plenty of kings who were Johns -- and , moreover , it is short , and sounds honest and manly . "
2282	2298	1588	1589	Mr Easy	129	" Yes , very true , my dear ; but they will call him Jack . "
2299	2335	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" Well , we have had several celebrated characters who were Jacks . There was -- let me see -- Jack the Giant Killer , and Jack of the Bean Stalk -- and Jack -- Jack-- "
2336	2340	2342	2343	Mrs Easy	131	" Jack Spratt , "
2345	2390	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" And Jack Cade , Mrs Easy , the great rebel -- and three - fingered Jack , Mrs Easy , the celebrated negro -- and , above all , Jack Falstaff , ma'am , Jack Falstaff -- honest Jack Falstaff -- witty Jack Falstaff-- "
2391	2409	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" I thought , Mr Easy , that I was to be permitted to choose the name . "
2410	2452	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" Well , so you shall , my dear ; I give it up to you . Do just as you please ; but depend upon it that John is the right name . Is it not now , my dear ? "
2453	2501	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" It 's the way you always treat me , Mr Easy ; you say that you give it up , and that I shall have my own way , but I never do have it . I am sure that the child will be christened John . "
2502	2538	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" Nay , my dear , it shall be just what you please . Now I recollect it , there were several Greek emperors who were Johns ; but decide for yourself , my dear . "
2539	2544	2546	2547	Mrs Easy	131	" No , no , "
2560	2614	2546	2547	Mrs Easy	131	" I give it up , Mr Easy . I know how it will be , as it always is : you give me my own way as people give pieces of gold to children , it 's their own money , but they must not spend it . Pray call him John . "
2615	2674	1656	1657	Mr Easy	129	" There , my dear , did not I tell you , you would be of my opinion upon reflection ? I knew you would . I have given you your own way , and you tell me to call him John ; so now we 're both of the same mind , and that point is settled . "
