3858	3864	3866	3867	Mrs Easy	131	" A very little one ! "
3869	3886	3841	3843	the young woman	452	" Yes , ma'am , very small indeed , and died soon after it was born . "
3887	3899	3841	3843	the young woman	452	" Oh , Dr Middleton!--what could you mean , Dr Middleton ? "
3900	3905	3907	3908	the doctor	441	" My dear madam , "
3915	4062	3907	3908	the doctor	441	" this is the only person that I could find suited to the wants of your child , and if you do not take her , I can not answer for its life . It is true that a married woman might be procured ; but married women who have a proper feeling will not desert their own children ; and , as Mr Easy asserts , and you appear to imagine , the temper and disposition of your child may be affected by the nourishment it receives , I think it more likely to be injured by the milk of a married woman who will desert her own child for the sake of gain . The misfortune which has happened to this young woman is not always a proof of a bad heart , but of strong attachment , and the overweening confidence of simplicity . "
4063	4070	4072	4073	Mr Easy	136	" You are correct , doctor , "
4075	4102	4072	4073	Mr Easy	136	" and her head proves that she is a modest young woman , with strong religious feeling , kindness of disposition , and every other requisite . "
4103	4125	3907	3908	the doctor	441	" The head may prove it all for what I know , Mr Easy , but her conduct tells another tale . "
4126	4137	4139	4140	the doctor	441	" She is well fitted for the situation , ma'am , "
